Shot.\"\r\n  TEXT HIT: 11a59fbe 'Liberty, Gellhorn, Alderney and Carcer had parachuted down into occupied Europe — either France or an even meeker country — and were immediately captured. They had escaped, killed over 5000 Arschlochkommandos in the process, before getting captured again. This time their prison camp had a fence, which made escape much harder.~n~~n~The Germans had rightfully identified Gellhorn as the main troublemaker, and put him in isolation, hoping to break his spirit. The mad Leonidan, however, soon turned the tables on his captors. Day in and day out, the guards outside his cell were driven mad by the unremitting sound of Gellhorn\\'s frenzied pumping, pausing only now and again for a breathless rendition of \"The Star-Spangled Banner\". When the last prison camp guard had finally succumbed — shrieking \"Nein!\" and shooting himself — Liberty had smartly identified his golden opportunity, commandeering their Übermacht motorbike and making an all-American jump straight through the fence. Loading up on guns, ammunition, explosives, cigars and Bratwurst, they were ready for phase three of the plan.~n~~n~Then there had been the hard and bloody tank battle at Panzerschlong. The surprisingly straightforward bombing of the dam at Wimpfken-Shmimpfken. The humbling moment of near defeat before the triumphant comeback at the compound in Klimaxburg.~n~~n~And then, the pièce de résistance: the final stage of their grand plan to win the war. At its heart, it was deceptively simple: the highest-ranking members of Germany\\'s political and military spheres were to be summoned to a remote château in the hills to attend a lavish dinner party hosted in celebration of the Führer himself. Except the Führer wouldn\\'t be there. Instead, those Krauts would be met by Captain Liberty, his squad, and enough dynamite to blow the Reich to hell and back and then back into hell again.~n~~n~By this point, Liberty\\'s life had almost finished flashing before his eyes. He caught final, fleeting glimpses of buxom French milkmaids with pails of cream, busty German waitresses'\r\n  TEXT HIT: 120ad52b 'Buy cosmetic upgrades for 5 sidearms and 5 longarms at Ammu-Nation.'\r\n  TEXT HIT: 1e84945c 'By Andrew Matoya~n~~n~With the number of crimes involving firearms steadily climbing across Leonida, gun control advocates are saying enough is enough, pointing to a recent study that reveals there are more guns in circulation in Leonida than people and their pets. However, Carson Perez, who leads the Leonida Senate Committee on Criminal Justice, believes the problem is not too many guns, but too few.~n~~n~Perez took questions on a new initiative he is spearheading, called \\'Guns 4 Gangsters\\', at a press conference held outside Ammu-Nation in Stockyard. \"It\\'s a bold move,\" admitted Perez, \"but we\\'re quietly confident that by enabling more criminals to have more access to firearms, we can significantly lower the number of gun-related crimes across the State.\"~n~~n~Trialing in Vice City, the Guns 4 Gangsters initiative will see galvanized steel boxes containing assorted firearms airdropped into crime hotspots and other sketchy neighborhoods. Perez explained: \"Did you know the best way to stop a kid smoking is to make him smoke and smoke until he\\'s sick? That\\'s what we\\'re doing here. We give every punk a firearm. They start off laughing, pointing the guns, even firing them. But the novelty wears off, they get sick of it, \n<truncated 74511 of 84399 bytes from the middle of the output>\ne9e68c\\\\scratch\\\\generate_mission_flow_mmd.py', 'C:\\\\Users\\\\<user>\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity-cli\\\\brain\\\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\\\\scratch\\\\generate_mission_flow_mmd.py.metadata.json', 'C:\\\\Users\\\\<user>\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity-cli\\\\brain\\\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\\\\scratch\\\\generate_named_mission_flow_mmd.py', 'C:\\\\Users\\\\<user>\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity-cli\\\\brain\\\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b1